<p class="footnote-item"><sup>2</sup> See Shabbos 88a — "<span class="key-term">nirdi nasan reicho</span>" — even the sin of the golden calf was transformed into a positive fragrance through Moshe's rebuke.</p>

<p class="footnote-item"><sup>3</sup> 32 threads × 2 (each twisted/doubled) = 64, + 8 threads themselves = 72 = <span class="key-term">Chesed</span>.</p>

<p class="footnote-item"><sup>4</sup> Menachos 43b — <span class="key-term">techeiles</span> resembles the sea, which resembles the sky, which resembles the <span class="key-term">Kisei HaKavod</span>.</p>

<p class="footnote-item"><sup>5</sup> Tikkunei Zohar, Tikkun 10 — the harp of David is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>.</p>

<p class="footnote-item"><sup>6</sup> <span class="zohar-quote">Kursaya d'dina</span> — the Zohar's term for the Throne of Judgment, corresponding to <span class="key-term">techeiles</span>.</p>

<p class="footnote-item"><sup>7</sup> The <span class="key-term">ba'al koach</span> (man of power) refers to the true <span class="key-term">tzaddik</span> whose prayer in the mode of judgment extracts vitality from the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span>. See Likutay Tinyana 8 at length.</p>

<p class="footnote-item"><sup>8</sup> The <span class="key-term">medameh</span> (imaginative faculty) is the interface between intellect and the physical world. It is the "garment" of the intellect — can reveal or conceal truth.</p>

<p class="footnote-item"><sup>9</sup> See Likutay Moharan I:7 — <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are conducive to <span class="key-term">emunah</span>.</p>

